</style>
<h2>Asobi Review 0.2 (build 559)</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Fixed: pasting a link you were sent could say "didn't parse".</b> Every shape of review link works now — and one that names you gives you your name, your watermark, and your notes attributed to you.</li>
<li><b>The Shared Review window says which way in is which.</b> <b>Someone sent you a link</b> comes first, since that's how a review or a delivered session usually arrives; <b>Someone is hosting nearby</b> is for the same network, with a passcode.</li>
<li><b>The web review carries the Autonomy mark</b> in its header, sitting on the line with the guide and the clock.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
